B. Simulator sickness
The simulator sickness analysis indicated moderate evidence for the absence of an effect of the driving simulator, BFincl = 0.24, and strong evidence for an effect of the driving scenario, BFincl = 1156.81 (Figure 8). Bayesian posthoc tests pointed out that signiﬁcantly more simulator sickness was induced in the urban scenario compared to all other scenarios. There was no interaction of visualization technology and scenario, BFincl = 0.09 (Figure 8).

